1
00:00:00,060 --> 00:00:02,500
[Minase]
Kairi-senpai.

2
00:00:02,500 --> 00:00:07,590
In the scene where they reunite,
their feelings are so complicated.

3
00:00:07,590 --> 00:00:11,260
I think Kengo still loves Yu.

4
00:00:11,260 --> 00:00:13,138
That's hot!

5
00:00:13,138 --> 00:00:14,568
Are you okay?

6
00:00:14,568 --> 00:00:16,248
Totally fine.

7
00:00:17,818 --> 00:00:20,278
Right, Kengo does.

8
00:00:20,278 --> 00:00:21,948
He's in love with Yu.

9
00:00:21,948 --> 00:00:27,068
And later,
there's a part where Kengo hugs Yu.

10
00:00:29,338 --> 00:00:30,868
Hug her...

11
00:00:31,828 --> 00:00:33,588
Kairi-senpai?

12
00:00:33,588 --> 00:00:37,488
Oh, no, it's nothing.

13
00:00:37,488 --> 00:00:39,458
Oh, right.

14
00:00:49,448 --> 00:00:51,168
I'll kill you.

15
00:00:51,988 --> 00:00:56,346
I'll kill you... I'll kill you...
I'll kill you... I'll kill you...

16
00:00:56,346 --> 00:00:58,016
I'll kill you...

17
00:01:00,188 --> 00:01:04,358
Whoa, this brings back memories.

18
00:01:04,358 --> 00:01:05,808
Look!

19
00:01:06,778 --> 00:01:08,988
Don't I look crazy with this face?

20
00:01:10,488 --> 00:01:14,238
You always pull a funny face
whenever the camera's on you.

21
00:01:14,238 --> 00:01:16,488
That's because it makes you laugh.

22
00:01:16,488 --> 00:01:19,628
I can't help but laugh.

23
00:01:30,648 --> 00:01:35,188
I wish we could go back to those days.

24
00:01:38,488 --> 00:01:40,548
If we could go back,

25
00:01:41,798 --> 00:01:44,798
I would never hurt you.

26
00:01:46,998 --> 00:01:50,118
You don't have to
worry about that anymore.

27
00:01:50,118 --> 00:01:52,478
If that never happened...

28
00:01:55,428 --> 00:01:58,328
would things be different between us?

29
00:02:17,638 --> 00:02:19,478
I'm in love with you,

30
00:02:20,428 --> 00:02:22,728
Ama.

31
00:02:22,728 --> 00:02:24,898
Ever since then.

32
00:02:26,098 --> 00:02:27,718
I've never...

33
00:02:29,278 --> 00:02:32,278
loved anyone this seriously.

34
00:02:45,918 --> 00:02:47,478
[Manager]
[New message]

35
00:02:47,478 --> 00:02:49,508
[We have a meeting tonight.]
[Seriously? Alright, got it.]

36
00:03:47,008 --> 00:03:51,138
I really appreciate your feelings,
Kairi-senpai.

37
00:03:52,198 --> 00:03:53,738
But...

38
00:03:59,338 --> 00:04:01,498
I knew it.

39
00:04:03,268 --> 00:04:05,038
I'm sorry.

40
00:04:06,198 --> 00:04:07,528
Oh...

41
00:04:09,541 --> 00:04:11,733
[Kengo: Oh, I'm sorry.]
It's like the script.

42
00:04:11,733 --> 00:04:16,253
Looks like I've really gotten
into this role, huh?

43
00:04:18,638 --> 00:04:20,838
Alright, let's get started.

44
00:04:20,838 --> 00:04:23,058
- Okay.
- Yeah, let's do this.

45
00:04:23,058 --> 00:04:24,918
- Open the script.
- Okay.

46
00:04:31,108 --> 00:04:33,308
If it weren't for that,

47
00:04:35,918 --> 00:04:38,528
would things be different between us?

48
00:04:40,108 --> 00:04:41,698
Kengo...

49
00:04:45,238 --> 00:04:48,068
<i>I threw myself into work</i>

50
00:04:48,068 --> 00:04:49,848
<i>so I could forget about Chiaki.</i>

51
00:04:49,848 --> 00:04:53,728
Ms. Rin, Mr. Asakura, Ms. Minase,
that's a wrap!

52
00:04:53,728 --> 00:04:55,568
That was great. See you next time.

53
00:04:55,568 --> 00:04:57,618
Thank you very much.

54
00:04:58,698 --> 00:05:01,978
I'm gonna miss seeing you.

55
00:05:01,978 --> 00:05:04,028
Keep being my friend, okay?

56
00:05:04,028 --> 00:05:06,628
Yes, let's stay friends.

57
00:05:06,628 --> 00:05:08,578
Thank you!

58
00:05:10,178 --> 00:05:11,826
Minase,

59
00:05:13,038 --> 00:05:14,968
do you have a moment after this?

60
00:05:14,968 --> 00:05:16,338
Yes?

61
00:05:19,818 --> 00:05:23,237
I got this from a weekly magazine
reporter today.

62
00:05:23,237 --> 00:05:24,818
[Love Triangle: Chiaki Hosho,
Kairi Asakura, and a New Actress?]

63
00:05:25,998 --> 00:05:28,118
Is this true?

64
00:05:30,718 --> 00:05:32,158
Yes.

65
00:05:34,158 --> 00:05:36,698
I'm so sorry.

66
00:05:37,298 --> 00:05:41,148
It's true that I was dating Mr. Hosho.

67
00:05:41,148 --> 00:05:44,928
But Mr. Asakura is just my senior.

68
00:05:48,008 --> 00:05:50,428
So, what should I do?

69
00:05:50,428 --> 00:05:54,548
A small agency like us can't do anything.

70
00:05:54,548 --> 00:05:57,728
The other agencies won't care.

71
00:05:57,728 --> 00:06:01,988
The only one who'll get hurt is you.

72
00:06:11,598 --> 00:06:14,048
Serves you right.

73
00:06:15,148 --> 00:06:17,298
How's work been lately?

74
00:06:19,005 --> 00:06:20,398
It's going well.

75
00:06:20,398 --> 00:06:22,848
I'm auditioning for a role soon.

76
00:06:23,488 --> 00:06:25,358
I see.

77
00:06:25,358 --> 00:06:27,858
When's Chiaki coming again?

78
00:06:27,858 --> 00:06:29,768
I wanna see him!

79
00:06:32,688 --> 00:06:34,724
[Weekly Times]

80
00:06:39,458 --> 00:06:44,518
[Popular Actor Chiaki Hosho's
Hidden Past with a Toxic Parent]

81
00:06:44,518 --> 00:06:46,168
What is this?

82
00:06:51,518 --> 00:06:54,318
<i>The article got pulled.</i>
[Manager]

83
00:06:56,458 --> 00:06:58,118
[Growing Up With a Toxic Parent]

84
00:06:58,118 --> 00:07:00,208
[Revenge Against His Mother?]

85
00:07:00,208 --> 00:07:04,008
<i>That's my mother. Hard to believe, right?</i>

86
00:07:04,908 --> 00:07:09,178
<i>Chiaki must be really hurt
after an article like this.</i>

87
00:07:19,038 --> 00:07:21,028
<i>We broke up, but...</i>

88
00:07:23,178 --> 00:07:27,658
<i>It's okay to worry about him
at a time like this, right?</i>

89
00:07:27,658 --> 00:07:29,118
<i>Hello?</i>

90
00:07:29,118 --> 00:07:30,778
Chiaki?

91
00:07:32,168 --> 00:07:35,858
<i>I saw the article...</i>

92
00:07:35,858 --> 00:07:37,508
You saw it?

93
00:07:40,318 --> 00:07:42,178
Are you okay?

94
00:07:48,178 --> 00:07:51,548
Yeah, I'm fine.

95
00:07:52,478 --> 00:07:55,748
Because I gave them that article.

96
00:07:56,688 --> 00:07:58,268
Why would you...

97
00:07:58,268 --> 00:07:59,888
<i>Hey, Ama.</i>

98
00:08:00,768 --> 00:08:03,028
Can we meet for a bit?

99
00:08:04,558 --> 00:08:06,888
I'm sorry.

100
00:08:06,888 --> 00:08:10,248
They wrote about me too recently.

101
00:08:10,248 --> 00:08:12,278
<i>Don't worry about that.</i>

102
00:08:13,038 --> 00:08:16,818
I'm the one who got your article taken down.

103
00:08:17,998 --> 00:08:20,038
What do you mean?

104
00:08:21,238 --> 00:08:24,428
So let's meet up, okay?

105
00:08:33,658 --> 00:08:35,438
Long time no see.

106
00:08:36,228 --> 00:08:37,958
You've been well?

107
00:08:39,718 --> 00:08:41,098
Yeah.

108
00:08:47,528 --> 00:08:49,768
First, let me apologize.

109
00:08:52,658 --> 00:08:54,528
I hurt you.

110
00:08:56,508 --> 00:08:57,898
I'm sorry.

111
00:09:02,268 --> 00:09:04,828
Before I met you,

112
00:09:05,728 --> 00:09:09,118
I was a truly terrible person.

113
00:09:11,658 --> 00:09:14,358
After what my mother did to me,

114
00:09:14,358 --> 00:09:17,598
I'd treat women as if I'm getting revenge.

115
00:09:18,978 --> 00:09:20,968
I'm also at fault...

116
00:09:22,238 --> 00:09:24,468
for not hearing you out.

117
00:09:25,868 --> 00:09:27,808
I'm sorry.

118
00:09:29,778 --> 00:09:31,688
But...

119
00:09:31,688 --> 00:09:34,078
I was really shocked.

120
00:09:37,588 --> 00:09:40,488
I trusted you, Chiaki.

121
00:09:41,078 --> 00:09:43,248
Because I loved you.

122
00:09:48,018 --> 00:09:50,968
I promise I'll never hurt you again.

123
00:09:54,118 --> 00:09:56,758
For the first time in my life...

124
00:09:57,768 --> 00:10:04,358
when I fell in love with you,
I realized how stupid I was.

125
00:10:06,658 --> 00:10:08,228
I'm sorry.

126
00:10:09,268 --> 00:10:12,238
You didn't come here to listen to this.

127
00:10:13,978 --> 00:10:18,998
Why did you give your own story
to the reporters?

128
00:10:21,858 --> 00:10:25,433
That article was supposed to be about me.
[Love Triangle: Chiaki Hosho, Kairi Asakura,]

129
00:10:25,433 --> 00:10:26,831
[and a New Actress?]

130
00:10:29,658 --> 00:10:33,358
When I heard that article
was getting published,

131
00:10:33,358 --> 00:10:35,538
I contacted the reporter.

132
00:10:37,348 --> 00:10:42,728
And they demanded something interesting
in exchange.

133
00:10:44,078 --> 00:10:45,518
But...

134
00:10:46,108 --> 00:10:49,058
- now you're...
- I don't care.

135
00:10:50,088 --> 00:10:52,568
I don't care what happens to me.

136
00:10:59,558 --> 00:11:01,898
You're working hard.

137
00:11:03,868 --> 00:11:06,068
I know that.

138
00:11:07,938 --> 00:11:11,298
I don't want your future ruined
by an article like that.

139
00:11:14,408 --> 00:11:16,108
Even now,

140
00:11:17,538 --> 00:11:19,938
I'll continue to support you.

141
00:11:22,608 --> 00:11:24,508
I'm sorry.

142
00:11:26,088 --> 00:11:28,028
Thank you.

143
00:11:37,798 --> 00:11:41,208
Chiaki, take this.

144
00:11:49,488 --> 00:11:51,008
Well then.

145
00:12:04,598 --> 00:12:08,248
Keep this with you.

146
00:12:12,508 --> 00:12:14,298
Even now,

147
00:12:15,788 --> 00:12:17,748
I still love you.

148
00:12:29,718 --> 00:12:32,308
<i>Ama. It's a cute name.</i>

149
00:12:32,308 --> 00:12:35,288
It's okay. I'm on your side.

150
00:12:35,288 --> 00:12:37,438
Go out with me.

151
00:12:39,028 --> 00:12:40,308
<i>I like you.</i>

152
00:12:40,308 --> 00:12:44,728
<i>You're kind, straightforward,
and you give it your all.</i>

153
00:12:46,248 --> 00:12:48,808
<i>I love you, truly.</i>

154
00:12:48,808 --> 00:12:52,488
<i>I should have done this sooner,
to make you mine alone.</i>

155
00:12:52,488 --> 00:12:57,368
<i>Before I met you,
I was a truly terrible person.</i>

156
00:12:57,368 --> 00:13:03,038
<i>When I fell in love with you,
I realized how stupid I was.</i>

157
00:13:03,038 --> 00:13:06,868
<i>You're working hard. I know that.</i>

158
00:13:06,868 --> 00:13:11,028
<i>I'll continue to support you.</i>

159
00:13:11,028 --> 00:13:14,208
<i>Even now, I still love you.</i>

160
00:13:25,818 --> 00:13:27,468
What happened?

161
00:13:30,838 --> 00:13:32,318
Ama?

162
00:13:33,918 --> 00:13:35,358
I...

163
00:13:36,788 --> 00:13:39,158
I want to stay by your side.

164
00:13:42,098 --> 00:13:43,818
Thank you.

165
00:13:45,318 --> 00:13:46,828
But,

166
00:13:47,798 --> 00:13:50,733
I didn't do this for your pity...

167
00:13:50,733 --> 00:13:52,623
It's not pity!

168
00:13:55,658 --> 00:13:57,218
Then...

169
00:13:58,138 --> 00:13:59,778
why?

170
00:14:07,888 --> 00:14:12,898
I still love you, Chiaki.

171
00:14:15,198 --> 00:14:17,878
I was shocked,

172
00:14:17,878 --> 00:14:20,388
and there are things I can't forgive,

173
00:14:21,778 --> 00:14:25,148
but I still want to stay
by your side forever.

174
00:14:29,418 --> 00:14:31,038
Ama...

175
00:14:42,598 --> 00:14:44,508
Are you really sure?

176
00:14:46,718 --> 00:14:48,058
Yeah.

177
00:15:24,258 --> 00:15:25,698
Ama.

178
00:15:28,288 --> 00:15:31,148
Thank you for coming back to me.

179
00:17:22,368 --> 00:17:24,668
<i>Want some advice?</i>

180
00:17:26,968 --> 00:17:30,138
Sacrifice yourself to save them

181
00:17:30,138 --> 00:17:35,838
when they're in trouble,
and make them feel guilty.

182
00:17:36,548 --> 00:17:40,688
Women easily mix up love and guilt.

183
00:17:41,538 --> 00:17:48,228
Love is all about taking advantage
of the other person.

184
00:17:51,648 --> 00:17:54,248
[What the hell? A magazine is running
a story about your fight with Kairi.]

185
00:17:54,248 --> 00:17:55,458
<i>Are you sure?</i>

186
00:17:55,458 --> 00:17:59,848
You can write it as horribly
and miserably as you want.

187
00:17:59,848 --> 00:18:02,928
You can't come back crying to me later.

188
00:18:02,928 --> 00:18:07,788
In exchange,
you'll never run that other article.

189
00:18:08,728 --> 00:18:12,218
Promise me.

190
00:18:21,188 --> 00:18:25,698
I love you... Ama.

191
00:18:33,488 --> 00:18:35,088
[Last White End]
[Project Proposal]

192
00:18:35,088 --> 00:18:38,168
It's Seira's first Japanese drama in a while.

193
00:18:38,168 --> 00:18:42,168
You've been offered a role
as her subordinate.

194
00:18:44,488 --> 00:18:46,377
It's a role with adultery, revenge, murder...

195
00:18:46,377 --> 00:18:48,288
Pretty tough stuff.

196
00:18:48,288 --> 00:18:50,058
I'll take it.

197
00:18:50,058 --> 00:18:51,668
All right, let's do this.

198
00:18:51,668 --> 00:18:53,008
Yes.

199
00:18:57,618 --> 00:19:00,578
Hey! Why isn't the article out?

200
00:19:00,578 --> 00:19:03,198
Well, your scoop's
just not interesting enough.

201
00:19:03,198 --> 00:19:06,628
Huh? You said it was a huge scoop!

202
00:19:06,628 --> 00:19:08,918
I paid you. Isn't that enough?

203
00:19:08,918 --> 00:19:10,698
Go home.

204
00:19:14,188 --> 00:19:17,658
Damn old man, don't mess with me.

205
00:19:32,398 --> 00:19:34,588
Too bad.

206
00:19:37,658 --> 00:19:39,278
That was you, right?

207
00:19:39,278 --> 00:19:42,848
Snooping around behind my back.

208
00:19:48,888 --> 00:19:51,588
What's this?

209
00:19:55,688 --> 00:19:58,378
With some old geezer like him,

210
00:19:58,378 --> 00:20:00,748
you must've had it real tough.

211
00:20:03,458 --> 00:20:07,348
You really are a scumbag!

212
00:20:08,838 --> 00:20:11,318
I'm just getting even.

213
00:20:13,568 --> 00:20:16,328
Someone like you,

214
00:20:17,268 --> 00:20:19,768
I could make disappear anytime.

215
00:20:20,388 --> 00:20:22,838
Don't come near Ama ever again.

216
00:20:22,838 --> 00:20:24,548
Understood?

217
00:20:26,338 --> 00:20:28,058
Answer me.

218
00:20:30,618 --> 00:20:32,568
I get it!

219
00:20:33,178 --> 00:20:37,238
So delete that, okay?

220
00:20:44,688 --> 00:20:47,518
Damn. What's wrong with him?

221
00:20:47,518 --> 00:20:49,988
He's way too dangerous.

222
00:20:58,007 --> 00:20:59,069
Huh?

223
00:20:59,069 --> 00:21:01,607
[Old Producer: Don't contact me.]
[Idol Fan: How much to sleep with me?]

224
00:21:03,168 --> 00:21:04,438
Why?

225
00:21:04,438 --> 00:21:06,279
[Manager Suzui]

226
00:21:11,928 --> 00:21:13,898
- Yes?
<i>- That stuff online.</i>

227
00:21:13,898 --> 00:21:16,728
<i>We need to talk. Come to the office now.</i>

228
00:21:16,728 --> 00:21:18,418
<i>Hurry up.</i>

229
00:21:25,758 --> 00:21:29,418
[Gross. She's sleeping with producers.]

230
00:21:29,418 --> 00:21:31,268
Why? Why?
[Blacklisted]

231
00:21:31,268 --> 00:21:33,478
[She's a goner, huh?]

232
00:21:33,478 --> 00:21:35,548
[Wait, who even is Anna Saotome?]

233
00:21:40,688 --> 00:21:45,058
Oh, a new drama?

234
00:21:45,058 --> 00:21:46,728
Good for you.

235
00:21:47,768 --> 00:21:49,718
Thank you.

236
00:21:58,018 --> 00:22:02,788
Are you worried about me?

237
00:22:05,248 --> 00:22:06,638
Yeah.

238
00:22:09,278 --> 00:22:11,988
It's okay.

239
00:22:11,988 --> 00:22:14,148
Even without work,

240
00:22:15,728 --> 00:22:21,198
spending quiet time like this with you
makes me happy.

241
00:22:55,578 --> 00:22:57,878
<i>So beautiful...</i>

242
00:22:57,878 --> 00:23:01,988
<i>Being in the same space as her
feels like a dream.</i>

243
00:23:05,808 --> 00:23:07,128
<i>Huh?</i>

244
00:23:11,968 --> 00:23:13,898
<i>She's coming to me?</i>

245
00:23:17,168 --> 00:23:19,088
Hello.

246
00:23:19,088 --> 00:23:21,298
Nice to meet you.

247
00:23:21,298 --> 00:23:24,838
You're Ama Minase, right?

248
00:23:24,838 --> 00:23:26,978
You know who I am?

249
00:23:26,978 --> 00:23:30,198
You're Chiaki's girlfriend now, aren't you?

250
00:23:30,198 --> 00:23:31,618
<i>Huh?</i>

251
00:23:33,388 --> 00:23:36,228
It must be hard for you.

252
00:23:36,228 --> 00:23:40,508
He's so possessive.

253
00:23:50,498 --> 00:23:52,708
You really are twisted.

254
00:23:52,708 --> 00:23:57,498
I could sell a scandal about that girl
for a pretty penny.

255
00:23:57,498 --> 00:24:00,298
I think we should break up.

